@@s058 At the exam
@@s059 At the exam
@@s060 Connectivity that grows over time, or Kruskal: write <i>"We maintain disjoint sets with union-find, using union by size and path compression; m operations cost O(m α(m, n))."</i>
@@s061 If the question asks to check whether two nodes are connected <b>just once</b>, a BFS is enough; if the edges arrive <b>one at a time</b> and the answer is needed after each edge, union-find.
